From: Velocor <noreply@velocor.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bdev/lvol: add bdev_lvol_snapshot_group

bdev_lvol_snapshot makes one lvol's snapshot consistent on its own, but there is no way to
snapshot several lvols at one point in time while hosts write to them: snapshots taken one
after another by separate RPCs each capture a different moment, so an application spreading
its data over several volumes (a database and its log, a VM with several disks) can't be
restored consistently. The NVMe-oF subsystem pause and bdev quiesce functions that could
order this exist in the C API but have no RPC, and pausing through separate RPCs would leave
I/O stalled if the caller died between them.

Add vbdev_lvol_create_snapshot_group() and the bdev_lvol_snapshot_group RPC, which do the
whole operation in one call: every member lvol bdev is quiesced (spdk_bdev_quiesce: I/O
submitted before completes, new I/O is queued), the snapshots are created one after another
once all are quiesced, then every bdev is unquiesced and the queued I/O runs. This works for
any front end (NVMe-oF, iSCSI, vhost, ublk) because it acts at the bdev layer. A descriptor is
held on each member for the duration, so a concurrent delete can't free a bdev under a
pending quiesce.

If the bdevs aren't all quiesced within quiesce_timeout_ms (default 5000; 0 for no limit, for
example a member whose I/O is stuck on a failing disk), no snapshot is taken: the members
already quiesced are unquiesced at once and the others as soon as their quiesce completes,
and the RPC fails with ETIMEDOUT. If a snapshot fails, the remaining ones aren't attempted,
everything is unquiesced, and the error names the snapshots that were taken so the caller can
delete them. The same lvol listed twice is refused (it would wait for itself).

  bdev_lvol_snapshot_group {"snapshots": [{"lvol_name": "...", "snapshot_name": "..."}, ...],
                            "quiesce_timeout_ms": 5000}
  result: the snapshots' UUIDs, in request order

Also: the schema entry, the rpc.py command and the RPC documentation.

Unit test: ut_lvol_snapshot_group.

Applies to SPDK v26.09 (0bbb7fe4dccfb31e8d446da8822360704949d1e9) after 0001 and 0002.
